> A caution about all five. Almost none of the planets' gearing survives. The gear ratios I used are those of a reconstruction published by Freeth and others in 2021. For Venus and Saturn, the two that do worse, the number of years in each ratio is read on the machine's inscriptions; for the three planets that do well the ratios were supplied by that paper, which notes that they were already known in Babylonian astronomy. So the three pointers that would be nearly as good as new are the three whose ratios the reconstruction had to restore.
